by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2x,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(-2x)}^{2}+{(-2y)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,{x}^{2}{y}^{2}(-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,(-{x}^{4}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}{y}^{4})\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "246b6bfe-20aa-55cc-b239-3304de81494f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415952} {:answer/id #uuid "72fa2757-f8e2-52c7-97eb-f3ea64fd0de1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415959} {:answer/id #uuid "a9391385-1fbe-53da-993e-c0f38007e6e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{2}{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415964} {:answer/id #uuid "abd564cc-a7f0-5f60-a224-edcb8733b99b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415965} {:answer/id #uuid "fa49e0e8-2a63-57cc-8df5-3f02f87ef7e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abd564cc-a7f0-5f60-a224-edcb8733b99b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415965} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a33e921-a9bc-5edf-9d0c-b149f91622e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415975}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e3b0ae8-2464-5f3a-ba5b-28ac6b071959" :question/math-academy-id "q-161326" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{2}y,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=-\\sqrt{2}x-y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 0$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\sqrt{2}x-y)=-\\sqrt{2},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\sqrt{2}x-y)=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(-\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\sqrt{2}y\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,2\\sqrt{2}y\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c28baa-1ba7-516d-8ddc-a39e22c2e598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6} (- 4 x^{2} - 2 x y)}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530661} {:answer/id #uuid "b90f9ed2-e3a2-59a7-8cbb-91660aed4aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5} (- 4 x^{2} - 2 x y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530711} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b8033d-fe9b-5eab-acb7-633a4021da70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x^{2} - 2 x y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530712} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf2cf83-b10d-5e3f-8876-9061d4146960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6} (- 4 x^{2} - 2 x y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530713} {:answer/id #uuid "c6dbe8d6-115c-5f27-8781-bfe1b46dde92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 24 x^{2} - 12 x y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbf2cf83-b10d-5e3f-8876-9061d4146960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6} (- 4 x^{2} - 2 x y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530713} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c8369a-e66a-5962-aabd-88116b6a7415" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530690}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3681ad8b-d269-5b68-8bae-a23d7eb16998" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x z,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2 x + y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-1\\le y\\le 0.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\,\\boxed{}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x + y)=2,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x + y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+(2)^2+(1)^2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- 2 x (2 x + y))\\cdot (\\sqrt{6})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- 4 x^{2} - 2 x y)\\cdot (\\sqrt{6})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\,\\sqrt{6} (- 4 x^{2} - 2 x y)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530672 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e7b9d5a-7e03-5e38-9759-f8396dd47858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1} (2 x^{5} - 8 x^{4} y + 16 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530675} {:answer/id #uuid "848e4bb8-3c6f-5901-a73b-17464aa41442" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x^{5} - 8 x^{4} y + 16 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3}}{\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530697} {:answer/id #uuid "8b297ed7-dc23-548f-ba27-1e2705fc62fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x^{5} - 8 x^{4} y + 16 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530701} {:answer/id #uuid "d3224c84-6992-551a-b884-974d22379047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1) (2 x^{5} - 8 x^{4} y + 16 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530722} {:answer/id #uuid "fe37ccb0-3c6f-5c5b-88a7-4e10abbde1a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2}} (2 x^{5} - 8 x^{4} y + 16 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e7b9d5a-7e03-5e38-9759-f8396dd47858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1} (2 x^{5} - 8 x^{4} y + 16 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530675} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dcc20d1-68ab-5472-b533-2127d041de08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "37c4cfa9-0446-5895-b8a2-fde2c5de0dbf" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=2 x z^{2} + 2 y z,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=- x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2}$ for $-2\\le x\\le -1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\boxed{}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})=- 2 x + 2 y,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})=2 x + 4 y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+(- 2 x + 2 y)^2+(2 x + 4 y)^2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(2 x (- x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})^{2} + 2 y (- x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2}))\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(2 x^{5} - 8 x^{4} y + 16 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1} (2 x^{5} - 8 x^{4} y + 16 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3})\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530674 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4affc6ff-45c8-5179-bd5e-1a4320f9b6ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 x^{4} y - 8 x^{3} y^{2} + 2 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} + 4 y^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530677} {:answer/id #uuid "6ca11778-2707-5355-a95b-fe82f12d000b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1} (4 x^{4} y - 8 x^{3} y^{2} + 2 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} + 4 y^{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530685} {:answer/id #uuid "8cea6829-8402-5ac1-80fa-03f848be6048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 x^{4} y - 8 x^{3} y^{2} + 2 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} + 4 y^{5}}{\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530703} {:answer/id #uuid "9a421fd4-15a1-5137-b6a6-c085d1e6d93e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2}} (4 x^{4} y - 8 x^{3} y^{2} + 2 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} + 4 y^{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530705} {:answer/id #uuid "eb2de9e7-d9b0-5bfe-89da-22592cf2f836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1) (4 x^{4} y - 8 x^{3} y^{2} + 2 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} + 4 y^{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ca11778-2707-5355-a95b-fe82f12d000b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1} (4 x^{4} y - 8 x^{3} y^{2} + 2 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} + 4 y^{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530685} :answer-field/id #uuid "849c497e-c623-50be-9e88-b051bc0aa5d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3c29642f-a472-5c91-80fe-7e7c9769bea9" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=- x z + y z^{2},$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\boxed{}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})=- 4 x + 2 y,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})=2 x + 4 y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+(- 4 x + 2 y)^2+(2 x + 4 y)^2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- x (- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2}) + y (- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})^{2})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(4 x^{4} y - 8 x^{3} y^{2} + 2 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} + 4 y^{5})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1} (4 x^{4} y - 8 x^{3} y^{2} + 2 x^{3} - 4 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y + 8 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} + 4 y^{5})\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00c42430-1fc9-5ab1-b3e4-e64439a50882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 4 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{2}) \\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530660} {:answer/id #uuid "22488b4b-6eaa-54e6-9321-a65255989526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 4 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{2}) ((x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530670} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc0684f-705b-5fb6-b62c-6f0630074787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 4 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{2}}{\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530702} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7631c1-1fd4-5d83-97c5-482b17777c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530727} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f0d205-7805-51c7-989c-6e86453e59c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2}} (- 4 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00c42430-1fc9-5ab1-b3e4-e64439a50882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 4 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{2}) \\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530660} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff828bf9-a44e-52b7-8d7c-2316b4735f4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56f59bc8-cc0f-5350-80f2-c0de11dad7ea" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x z,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2 x^{2} + x y + 2 y^{2}$ for $-2\\le x\\le -1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\boxed{}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x^{2} + x y + 2 y^{2})=4 x + y,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x^{2} + x y + 2 y^{2})=x + 4 y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+(4 x + y)^2+(x + 4 y)^2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- 2 x (2 x^{2} + x y + 2 y^{2}))\\cdot (\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- 4 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{2})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,(- 4 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{2}) \\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "158319bc-7d97-54a9-9c8c-00fa9f9f1131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 2 x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3}}{\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530664} {:answer/id #uuid "1f325e7a-fc7c-5e31-b18c-1ff7e58c9867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 2 x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3}) ((- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530669} {:answer/id #uuid "7b970496-f099-5df8-af2c-245bce78602c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530694} {:answer/id #uuid "cdaf1f79-3b80-53cc-a7ff-ac2bee8a536a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2}} (- 2 x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530720} {:answer/id #uuid "ebefaff7-5fd7-553e-8174-a671c0226808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 2 x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3}) \\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebefaff7-5fd7-553e-8174-a671c0226808" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- 2 x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3}) \\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530729} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd8a9cfc-81d7-56d2-94ce-8ba42aeb00e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7cf04f8d-cbbc-5cd2-a0b9-c0c29878e1a9" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=2 y z,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=- x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2}$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-1\\le y\\le 0.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\,\\boxed{}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})=- 2 x + 2 y,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})=2 x + 4 y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+(- 2 x + 2 y)^2+(2 x + 4 y)^2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(2 y (- x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2}))\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- 2 x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\,(- 2 x^{2} y + 4 x y^{2} + 4 y^{3}) \\sqrt{(- 2 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75d50c07-52e9-53af-ae4f-7c65062b2c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- x^{3} - x^{2} y + 2 x y^{2}}{\\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530692} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa56657-0b7c-57cd-b3d4-53acf6a376c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x^{3} - x^{2} y + 2 x y^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530704} {:answer/id #uuid "a12c8347-2dc1-5d6b-8b0b-b2cf864f7062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- x^{3} - x^{2} y + 2 x y^{2}) \\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530708} {:answer/id #uuid "bfea963c-7d6f-5d6a-839e-8c0a21277a95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- x^{3} - x^{2} y + 2 x y^{2}) ((- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x + 4 y)^{2} + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530716} {:answer/id #uuid "c205008f-927e-5b6e-87af-235f36a0af42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x + 4 y)^{2}} (- x^{3} - x^{2} y + 2 x y^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530717}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a12c8347-2dc1-5d6b-8b0b-b2cf864f7062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- x^{3} - x^{2} y + 2 x y^{2}) \\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530708} :answer-field/id #uuid "75785d57-a37f-567b-b726-adc808a7eda5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "854069e0-c8d5-5b8c-a346-937