$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- x^{2} - x y - 2 y^{2})=- 2 x - y,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- x^{2} - x y - 2 y^{2})=- x - 4 y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+(- 2 x - y)^2+(- x - 4 y)^2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(x (- x^{2} - x y - 2 y^{2}))\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x - 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- x^{3} - x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x - 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\,(- x^{3} - x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2}) \\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x - 4 y)^{2} + 1}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "164b9d32-3649-5cfb-a653-b45f00d604a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- 4 x^{4} y - 4 x^{3} y^{2} - 4 x^{3} - 9 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 4 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5}}{\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530665} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6165ab-e353-54b6-9df3-e1f48138c116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "((x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1) (- 4 x^{4} y - 4 x^{3} y^{2} - 4 x^{3} - 9 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 4 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530667} {:answer/id #uuid "45831d40-d6af-5f84-ae4f-5f8fa603f7d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2}} (- 4 x^{4} y - 4 x^{3} y^{2} - 4 x^{3} - 9 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 4 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530676} {:answer/id #uuid "9d1c9a65-d5e4-574a-a9cc-25fbe390d5e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1} (- 4 x^{4} y - 4 x^{3} y^{2} - 4 x^{3} - 9 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 4 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530707} {:answer/id #uuid "c87326c4-e7ad-5b11-98d1-d385a30d2c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 x^{4} y - 4 x^{3} y^{2} - 4 x^{3} - 9 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 4 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d1c9a65-d5e4-574a-a9cc-25fbe390d5e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1} (- 4 x^{4} y - 4 x^{3} y^{2} - 4 x^{3} - 9 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 4 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530707} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b9fd5b3-cb52-5183-bd4d-ed236e148eb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e5df7328-b63c-5ba1-bc0f-fc1fa9ad47e6" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x z - y z^{2},$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=2 x^{2} + x y + 2 y^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\boxed{}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x^{2} + x y + 2 y^{2})=4 x + y,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2 x^{2} + x y + 2 y^{2})=x + 4 y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+(4 x + y)^2+(x + 4 y)^2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- 2 x (2 x^{2} + x y + 2 y^{2}) - y (2 x^{2} + x y + 2 y^{2})^{2})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- 4 x^{4} y - 4 x^{3} y^{2} - 4 x^{3} - 9 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 4 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\sqrt{(x + 4 y)^{2} + (4 x + y)^{2} + 1} (- 4 x^{4} y - 4 x^{3} y^{2} - 4 x^{3} - 9 x^{2} y^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 4 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5})\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0971b17f-ad93-5580-ba93-06499fcf447c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{- x^{4} y - 2 x^{3} y^{2} - x^{3} - 5 x^{2} y^{3} - x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5}}{\\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x - 4 y)^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530662} {:answer/id #uuid "38ad9d64-f81a-517e-bcc1-525559a3b57c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- x^{4} y - 2 x^{3} y^{2} - x^{3} - 5 x^{2} y^{3} - x^{2} y - 4 x y^{4} - 2 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530673} {:answer/id #uuid "5577374c-917