ned by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- x^{2} - x y + 2 y^{2})=- 2 x - y,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- x^{2} - x y + 2 y^{2})=- x + 4 y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+(- 2 x - y)^2+(- x + 4 y)^2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(x (- x^{2} - x y + 2 y^{2}) - y (- x^{2} - x y + 2 y^{2})^{2})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- x^{4} y - 2 x^{3} y^{2} - x^{3} + 3 x^{2} y^{3} - x^{2} y + 4 x y^{4} + 2 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\,\\sqrt{(- 2 x - y)^{2} + (- x + 4 y)^{2} + 1} (- x^{4} y - 2 x^{3} y^{2} - x^{3} + 3 x^{2} y^{3} - x^{2} y + 4 x y^{4} + 2 x y^{2} - 4 y^{5})\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "135b727b-90a5-58f3-b28d-73bc883b71d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2}) \\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530663} {:answer/id #uuid "1b855307-7285-5bec-af0e-c68f5677735c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530668} {:answer/id #uuid "6d953e63-3844-5dda-bebb-b265d30d5e52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2}} (2 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530686} {:answer/id #uuid "7897076e-28dc-5d0e-b8bb-01136fb78143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2}) ((- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530693} {:answer/id #uuid "e5cf50ea-4319-5a4f-ba19-0ba8b226670e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2}}{\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "135b727b-90a5-58f3-b28d-73bc883b71d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2}) \\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530663} :answer-field/id #uuid "172c374d-031f-5a6c-9d2b-39412dfe32ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f47f306f-a5eb-5b1d-8c05-eca24441fbf6" :question/problem "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=- x z,$ where the surface $S$ is defined by $z=- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below. \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\boxed{}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})=- 4 x + 2 y,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2})=2 x + 4 y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+(- 4 x + 2 y)^2+(2 x + 4 y)^2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(- x (- 2 x^{2} + 2 x y + 2 y^{2}))\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(2 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2})\\cdot (\\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,(2 x^{3} - 2 x^{2} y - 2 x y^{2}) \\sqrt{(- 4 x + 2 y)^{2} + (2 x + 4 y)^{2} + 1}\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals"}]}
